:DECLARE nCount :DEFAULT 0; writes the default inline on the :DECLARE
statement. It does not compile: no `;` ends the :DECLARE list before
:DEFAULT. diag.default_on_declare_line reports the :DEFAULT keyword
(issue #323, a v0.25.0 regression that validated clean).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE StartCount;
	:DECLARE nCount :DEFAULT 0;
	nCount := nCount + 1;
	:RETURN nCount;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE StartCount;
	:DECLARE nCount :DEFAULT 0;

	nCount := nCount + 1;

	:RETURN nCount;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
2:18-2:26 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' cannot initialize a ':DECLARE' list - ':DECLARE' takes only names, so this does not compile; give the variable its value with an assignment on the next line
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
